A weathered wooden wheel lying half-submerged in sand, with five distinct sections visible like pie slices, each segment showing a different state of decay—from freshly carved and golden on one end, through graying and cracking middle portions, to moss-covered and crumbling sections returning to earth. Around the wheel, scattered obsolete objects partially buried: a rusted gear, a faded circuit board, an ancient compass. In the background, fresh green shoots emerge from the sandy soil near the most decayed section, suggesting renewal. The scene is bathed in soft golden hour light, with dramatic shadows emphasizing texture. Rendered in Vincent van Gogh's distinctive style with bold, swirling brushstrokes, rich impasto technique, vibrant yellows and deep blues contrasting, expressive movement in the sky above, and emotional intensity in every curved line of the composition.
